    "en": "<p>Predictive performance in temporal learning depends on the learner <em>and</em> on the observation protocol that produced the data. The paper asks whether the joint measurement–target law under the <strong>realised</strong> protocol determines the predictive value of an <strong>undeployed</strong> alternative — counterfactual protocol evaluation (Section 1).</p>",
